Z||000003||Songman||08-06-2001||05:09 PM||||MY BEST FRIEND!!!<P>I hate to say it but I had hoped that you would take my lame attempt and do it the right way! <P>I love what you did with the red stripe. In mine the front and rear fascias would have had to have been modified. I am building THIS car! The only difference is that my molding will be white as on the original track Pace cars. And since I am building a clone I am having custome lettering done. I don't want it to look original. Actually, I bought two Indy wing fender badges from a 94 Cobra pace car. Same thing as ours but gold and chrome.. Is gonna be sweet!<P>I hope to be ordering my scoops and rockers soon. I think I am going to take and old notchback and start trying to do something like you have in the picture with the rounded rear edge on the side panel. Not sure if that is still in your plan. If it is let me know and I'll save myself some time. I was thinking of just getting rid of the side windows and just putting a black panel there with a vent in the rear. That may have been your plan as well... <P>Looking for the tail too! You know we aren't trying to push you.. we just love what you do!<P>I appreciate it more than you know, Jim...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
